Example: a cash deposit is a contribution, not investment profit.
The only selected holding is Assets:Cash in USD. The journal adds 100 USD on
2024-01-01, so the closing value and net contributions are both 100 USD.
Profit/loss is ending value 100 minus opening value 0 minus contributions 100 = 0.
The daily value equals the contribution, so the time-weighted return is 0.
The money-weighted returns cannot be calculated: all investor cash flows fall
on one date. The text formatter shows their null API values as n/a.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['Assets:Cash'], commodities: ['USD'], from: '2024-01-01', to: '2024-01-01' })

========== API FORMAT ==========

text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
account Assets:Cash
account Equity:Opening

2024-01-01 Deposit
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Equity:Opening  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2024-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: 100.00 USD
Ending value: 100.00 USD
Profit/loss: 0.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 0.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): n/a
Money-weighted return (annualized): n/a

========== WARNINGS ==========
